{"change_summary":"Implemented the remaining budget-tracking amendments on HEAD. The structural coverage guard now recognizes top-level implicit-biomass animal `*_count` fields while explicitly excluding `animal.berried_females_count`, with matching `AnimalState` documentation. Added the water-change residue bookkeeping comment, strengthened the canonical total-helper tests so particulate and fine detritus are verified separately, and reworked the daily plant/algae loss routing so those biomass losses now go to `fine_detritus_g_total` instead of dissolving directly into `DOC`/`DON`. Regression coverage now asserts the plant/algae/periphyton loss paths stay particulate while total N/C remain conserved.","outstanding_risks":["Daily `plant_respiration_fraction_per_day` and `algae_respiration_fraction_per_day` are now modeled as particulate turnover in the daily biomass pass; if a later phase wants literal organism-respiration bookkeeping at that stage, the parameter naming/docs and O2/DIC coupling should be revisited together.","The structural coverage guard remains convention-based. Future explicit N/C pools with non-standard names, or new top-level animal `*_count` fields that are bookkeeping-only rather than biomass-bearing, will require updating the discovery rules and docs together.","Complex multi-process stages such as `system:nitrogen_cycle` still rely on snapshot-derived gross component budgets, so same-component turnover inside one stage can remain collapsed until those stages emit explicit source/sink deltas.","The worktree still contains unrelated untracked content in `.ralph-burning/`."],"steps":[{"description":"Audited the pending amendments against the current `tank_core` budget helpers, structural coverage rules, water-change bookkeeping, and daily plant/algae routing to confirm which gaps still existed on HEAD.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Updated the budget-path coverage support code and tests: documented the implicit-mass animal count convention in `AnimalState`, taught the structural test to recognize future top-level animal `*_count` pools while excluding `berried_females_count`, and split the detritus assertions in the canonical total-helper tests so particulate and fine detritus are validated independently.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Patched the runtime bookkeeping: added the non-budget residue-shadow comment in `water_change.rs` and rerouted daily plant/algae loss terms from direct dissolved-organic routing into `fine_detritus_g_total`, with regression assertions that DOC/DON no longer increase on those paths.","order":3,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Formatted the workspace and ran focused plus full-package validation to confirm the amended routing and helper coverage pass cleanly.","order":4,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all` completed after the code changes.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test budget_tracking -- --nocapture` passed (18 tests), including the updated helper-coverage, detritus-split, and particulate-routing regressions.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test plant_algae_integration -- --nocapture` passed (8 tests).","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed across the full `tank_core` suite.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core -- -D warnings` passed."]}